## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Platform Priority**: Should we develop for Mobile-first, PC-first, or simultaneously? This affects input system design priority (touch vs keyboard) and performance budgets.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Engine Confirmation**: Do you want to use Unity (recommended) or Godot? This locks the entire tech stack before Phase 1 begins.

> [!NOTE]
> **Handcrafted vs Procedural for MVP**: The doc requires 20 handcrafted levels. Do you want these designed in a level editor (Unity Tilemap editor) or auto-generated with manual curation/override?

> [!NOTE]
> **Multiplayer Timeline**: Photon Fusion multiplayer is listed as "Future Mode." Should this be scoped into Phase 4, or deferred entirely to a post-launch update?

> [!TIP]
> **Art Assets**: Will you commission custom neon tile art, or use Unity's built-in tile assets + custom shaders to achieve the circuit-board neon aesthetic described in the doc?

---

## Verification Plan

### After Phase 1
- Arrow moves through a generated maze without clipping
- Direction locking prevents instant reversal
- Momentum system accelerates and decelerates correctly
- Camera follows player and minimap renders

### After Phase 2
- Dynamic pathways open/close on timer and signal trigger
- Hazards kill player and respawn logic works
- All 4 game modes are selectable from main menu
- Adaptive difficulty adjusts trap timing after 3+ consecutive deaths

### After Phase 3
- All 20 handcrafted levels are completable
- FMOD audio layers react to player speed and danger
- Corruption Zone shader applies visual glitch correctly
- 60fps maintained on target mobile hardware

### After Phase 4
- Daily challenge seeds are fetched from Firebase and deterministic
- Leaderboard entries are submitted and displayed
- In-app purchases flow works in test environment
- Ghost playback runs alongside live player correctly
